      "writtenOn": "2026-04-10T14:51:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a comment to the future, \"character\" here is not a great name, it is more legacy and is closer to how OpenType documents the cmap Format 14 table. If fully going with OpenType names here, this \"CMapEntry\" is a \"UVS\" (Unicode Variation Sequence) which consists of a \"base character\" and a \"variation selector\". However, it is also used for non-UVS (no variation selector) purposes. The naming here is something of a compromise.\n\nFrom a user (and maybe even implementation) point of view it might make sense to just allow a string of UTF-8 here. However, while putting together this interface it seemed best to make this extremely explicit.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "723f0370039412eef938102edf7c9084278a3aec",
